f your head  and then after you go dark with  jennifer's body  you can uh sort of boost your mood with  harry elfont and deborah kaplan's 2001  live-action  adaptation of josie and the pussycats it  is like a perfect counterpoint about  friendship it stars rachel  cook rosario dawson tara reed as josie  and the pussycats it was similarly  dismissed but  has endured thanks to its radiant  positivity  an excellent soundtrack that i still  listen to to this day  and really subtly sly social commentary  that tackles  manipulative marketing corporate  feminism and ultimately like  how the pure power of friendship can  literally save the world and even if it  wasn't just such a pure delight it would  be  worth watching to see parker posey and  alan [ __ ] having the time  of their lives as the antagonist but it  really ticks all the boxes and it's just  brimming with infectious enthusiasm  giddy glittery  antics and it's all just the right  amount of camp why do you do  what you do to me baby yep okay see  i just wanted to prove i knew what you  were talking about i never thought about  it as a midnight movie before  i think that it ended up there because  the audience had to find itself right  like it could have been  easily a matinee movie for a bigger  audience but because it wasn't accepted  the right way  it sort of built the subculture around  it it's perfect for like rocking out at  midnight with your friends  you're right and and i think the musical  element it makes sense in the sort of  midnight movie thing when you look at  like a rocky horror picture show  and you want your whole audience  engaging and singing and stuff like that  and also the characters of so many good  one-liners in that movie  i i can't believe people didn't think it  was as funny as it is when it came out  because it makes me  cackle it's great for the midnight movie  vibe like the costumes are so  flourishy and over the top you could  totally dress up for it if you went to a  theater  when those things are happening again  with your friends and be all glittery  and gaudy  just an audience full of those cat ears  that they're like trying to sell in the  movie  but that brings up an interesting point  so what do you think makes  a great midnight movie so i do think  that  josie is a really good example because i  think it is sort of about the  subculture what community that builds up  around these films you know the practice  really took off in the 70s as all the  the daytime slots were taken up by  more mainstream blockbusters family  films award contenders that kind  of movie that everyone wants to go see  the four quadrant films if you will  theaters discovered that they could get  a new audience in later  by showing more provocative off the  beaten path films and  out of that there really did come this  sense of community among midnight films  that you still find to this day it's why  rocky horror has this legendary  decades-long run  of these midnight events same for the  big lebowski has themed events all the  time  they spring up a subculture in a  community around the film and i think  midnight movie even as a descriptor  speaks  more to that community than the content  of the films themselves because they can  be anything they can be horror musicals  comedies  and it's about the community that comes  up around them rather than trying to say  well midnight movies have to be camping  they have to be  b movies it's really up to the audience  to decide i think  that was so well put i love it but i was  expecting to be like  it's gotta be funny you know i don't  know but that was  i love it well thank you so much haley  for coming on the show where can people  find you you can always find me on  collider you can find me on twitter  haleyfuch you can find me on instagram  at haystackmacgroovy  we have a weekly horror podcast called  the witching hour that i host with the  lovely perry nemeroff  i'm easy to find what's a good horror  midnight movie 